  "id": "interresponse-time",
  "term": "interresponse time",
  "definition": "Interresponse time is the elapsed time between one response and the next. In this source, it is discussed as the time since the most recent response, which can act as a controlling variable for choice behavior under concurrent reinforcement schedules.",
